<% content_for :title, "Simple Interest Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  Simple Interest calculator page (spec issue #78, DESIGN.md BLEND). Compute interest
  charged only on the original principal (never compounded):
    interest = principal × (rate / 100) × time_in_years
    total    = principal + interest
  Time is entered with a unit (Years | Months); months convert to years before the formula.

  The form posts over Turbo and re-renders the #result region in place; it works WITHOUT
  JS — the server validates the inputs and the checked inputs[unit] radio, and re-renders
  the result fragment. Unlike Percentage/BMI, no field depends on the chosen unit, so the
  Stimulus controller is pure polish: it only lifts the active segmented-control half. The
  no-JS baseline is unchanged — peer:checked paints the active half before JS connects.

  Unit picker — N = 2 short labels (Years | Months) → per DESIGN.md §4 it is a SEGMENTED
  CONTROL (the connected horizontal track, reusing the .direction-pill vocabulary), NOT a
  wrapping pill row or the .mode-option list. A native radio <fieldset>/<legend> posts
  inputs[unit].

  Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), collapsing to
  one column on mobile. Spacing scale ("targets not minimums"):
    • unit segmented control → halves tight on the Affix tier (gap-1)
    • stacked fields    → space-y-5
    • mode → fields → submit (major blocks) → mt-8 (Section tier)
    • column gutters / card padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout tier)
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Financial</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Simple Interest Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Interest charged only on the original principal — never compounded. Enter a principal,
    an annual rate, and a term in years or months, and see the interest accrued and the
    ending balance. Every answer is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/simple_interest", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "simple-interest" } do |f| %>

      <%# Fields. Principal carries a $ affix, rate a % affix (Affix tier — gap-2, the
          symbol next to its field, DESIGN.md §3). Stacked tier: space-y-5 down the column. %>
      <div class="space-y-5">
        <%# Principal — money, with a leading $ affix. %>
        <div>
          <%= f.label :principal, "Principal", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_principal" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :principal, id: "inputs_principal", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Annual rate — percent, with a trailing % affix. %>
        <div>
          <%= f.label :rate, "Annual rate", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_rate" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :rate, id: "inputs_rate", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">%</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Time + unit. The amount and its unit are parts of one control (DESIGN.md §3 —
            the Time field and its Years|Months segmented control read together). %>
        <div>
          <%= f.label :time, "Time", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_time" %>
          <%= f.number_field :time, id: "inputs_time", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                min: "0", placeholder: "0", class: "field-input mt-1.5" %>

          <%# Unit picker — a mode/variant picker with N=2 short options, so per DESIGN.md
              §4 it is a SEGMENTED CONTROL: one connected horizontal track, the two options
              as halves, the active half lifted to surface white. Reuses the segmented-
              control vocabulary (.direction-pill) on the bg-tinted bordered track, halves
              tight on the Affix tier (gap-1, parts of one control). Native radio
              <fieldset>/<legend> with peer sr-only radios posting inputs[unit]; the active
              half is painted by peer:checked (no-JS baseline) and .is-active (the Stimulus
              paintUnit hook), so it works without JS. %>
          <fieldset class="mt-2">
            <legend class="sr-only">Time unit</legend>
            <div class="flex gap-1 rounded-[11px] border border-border-input bg-bg p-1">
              <% [["years", "Years"], ["months", "Months"]].each_with_index do |(value, text), i| %>
                <%= f.radio_button :unit, value,
                      checked: i.zero?,
                      class: "peer sr-only",
                      data: { simple_interest_target: "unitInput", action: "simple-interest#select" } %>
                <%= f.label :unit, text, value: value,
                      class: "direction-pill",
                      data: { simple_interest_target: "pill", unit: value } %>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </fieldset>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
